      "answerSource": "derived",
      "answerKeyRef": null,
      "explanation": "Let the present ages be F and S. Ten years ago F−10 = 4(S−10), so F = 4S−30. Ten years hence F+10 = 2(S+10), so F = 2S+10. Solving gives S = 20 and F = 50. Check: 40 = 4 × 10 and 60 = 2 × 30. Verified solution (unofficial); original printed paper and worked derivation checked on 26 October 2026.",
